# Target C — KKT force-hull / reciprocal-geometry route

Target C is the third active endgame for Erdős Problem #99. It starts directly from global diameter optimality and the normalized KKT system rather than from Target A's independent scaffold/Hall response or Target B's almost-rhombic shell decomposition.

**LEVEL I STATUS: STILL OPEN.**

## Controlling update — 2026-09-09

Read [56 — C-I restored; C-II remains](56-ci-restored-frontier.md) before the
older frontier below. The promoted
[orientation/dependency audit](../../reports/target_c_c53_orientation_and_ci_restoration_2026-09-09.md)
withdraws the incorrectly normalized pentagon regression, restores C53 universal
selected-stress PSD and C63 finite integration, and closes C-I. A hypothetical
counterexample has a contact/diameter-lexicographically minimal representative
with `C=C_*` and `H=H_*`. C-II remains open, including the isolated-point population.
Older statements below that C-I or universal PSD remain unproved are superseded
only to this extent; later C-II claims are not automatically promoted.

### Promoted cross-target integrator update

The [shared ambient-force/cap module](../../theory/04-ambient-force-and-cap-transport.md)
gives `R(F)<=D/2+O(sqrt(D))` for every selected force hull by inclusion in
the actual global source hull. Thus every normalized stress has
`P_*=2D-O(sqrt(D))`; all actual diameter-star angles are `O(D^(-1/4))`.
Normalized force-hull limits are centrally symmetric cyclic hulls, with limiting
area/perimeter relation `a>=p-3pi/4`. Exterior population satisfies
`Z_ext=(pi D^2/4-area(F))/(sqrt(3)/2)+O(D)` with explicit finite bounds.
These supersede the corresponding older circumradius warnings and fixed-angle
asymptotic summaries, but imply neither a matching nor few interior isolates.
The post-ZF `0.618470...` area and `0.593235...` surplus specializations remain
conditional reports.

